  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0248' contains 9 tables. The tables are User, Article, Book, Activity, Video_Interview, User_Comments, Book_Recommendation, Activity_Lottery, and User_Activity_Participation.\nThe User table represents a user of the system and contains columns for the user's last login time, password, registration time, role, user ID, and username. All columns allow null values. The User_ID is the primary key.\nThe Article table represents an article in the system and contains columns for the article's ID, author, content, publish time, and title. All columns allow null values. The Article_ID is the primary key.\nThe Book table represents a book in the system and contains columns for the book's author, description, ID, and title. All columns allow null values. The Book_ID is the primary key.\nThe Activity table represents an activity in the system and contains columns for the activity's description, ID, name, and time. All columns allow null values. The Activity_ID is the primary key.\nThe Video_Interview table represents a video interview in the system and contains columns for the publish time, title, and video link. All columns allow null values. The Video_ID is the primary key.\nThe User_Comments table represents user comments on articles and contains columns for the article ID, comment content, comment time, and user ID. The User_ID and Article_ID are foreign keys referencing the User and Article tables respectively.\nThe Book_Recommendation table represents book recommendations and contains columns for the book ID, review, recommendation reason, recommendation time, and recommender ID. The Book_ID and Recommender_ID are foreign keys referencing the Book and User tables respectively.\nThe Activity_Lottery table represents activity lotteries and contains columns for the activity ID, prize name, and winner ID. The Activity_ID and Winner_ID are foreign keys referencing the Activity and User tables respectively.\nThe User_Activity_Participation table represents user activity participations and contains columns for the activity ID, participation time, and user ID. The User_ID and Activity_ID are foreign keys referencing the User and Activity tables respectively.\nThis schema ensures referential integrity by enforcing foreign key constraints. It also ensures entity integrity by ensuring that each table has a primary key and that primary keys are unique and not null. It also ensures domain integrity by ensuring that the data types of the columns match the expected data type.",
  "gold_question": "The system is a user-article sharing forum with the following features:\n1.User Interaction Features:\nEach user has a unique User ID, Username, Password, Registration Time, Last Login Time, and Role.\nA user can participate in multiple activities, engage in video interviews, and comment or recommend books and articles.\n2.Content Management:\nThe system manages several books and articles.\nBook Information: Each book has a Book ID, Title, Author, and Description.\nArticle Information: Each article has an Article ID, Title, Content, Author, and Publish Time.\nActivity Information: Each activity has an Activity ID, Activity Name, Activity Time, and Description.\nVideo Interview Information: Each video interview has a Video ID, Title, Video Link, and Publish Time.\n3.Activity Management:\nThe system can organize source code reading activities, record activity names, times, and descriptions.\nUsers can participate in multiple activities.\nThe system also handles lottery activities, recording winner information and awarding gifts.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0248.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0248\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_login_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `registration_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `article` (\n  `article_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publish_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`article_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `activity` (\n  `activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`activity_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `video_interview` (\n  `video_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publish_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `video_link` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`video_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_comments` (\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `article_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `comment_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `comment_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`article_id`) REFERENCES `article` (`article_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book_recommendation` (\n  `recommendation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `book_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `recommender_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `review` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `recommendation_reason` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `recommendation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`recommendation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_recommendation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `book_recommendation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`recommender_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `activity_lottery` (\n  `lottery_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `prize_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `winner_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`lottery_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `activity_lottery_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`activity_id`) REFERENCES `activity` (`activity_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `activity_lottery_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`winner_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_activity_participation` (\n  `participation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `activity_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `participation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`participation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_activity_participation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_activity_participation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`activity_id`) REFERENCES `activity` (`activity_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
